---
title: Flow 2 — Lecturer Grades a Submission
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor Lecturer
    participant Client as Angular SPA
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant IAM as Identity and Access
    participant GRADE as Assignment and Grading
    participant ENR as Enrollment
    participant MQ as Message Broker
    participant NOTIF as Notification
    participant ANALYTICS as Analytics and Reporting

    Lecturer->>Client: Enter marks, click "Save Grade"
    Client->>GW: PUT /submissions/{id}/grade {marks, feedback} (JWT)
    GW->>IAM: validate token
    IAM-->>GW: valid, role = Lecturer
    GW->>GRADE: forward grade request

    GRADE->>ENR: confirm student is enrolled in this course
    ENR-->>GRADE: enrollment confirmed

    GRADE->>GRADE: save Grade record, mark submission Graded
    GRADE-->>GW: 200 OK
    GW-->>Client: Grade saved
    Client-->>Lecturer: "Grade saved"

    GRADE-)MQ: publish GradePosted (async)
    MQ-)NOTIF: consume GradePosted
    NOTIF->>NOTIF: notify student their grade is ready
    MQ-)ANALYTICS: consume GradePosted
    ANALYTICS->>ANALYTICS: recompute class average, update dashboard snapshot

    Note over GRADE,ANALYTICS: Grading itself never waits on Notification or Analytics —<br/>both consume the same event independently and in parallel
